## Experience and Lessons
|Case|:user_registration  
Pseudocode from Project 1:  
```python
CLASS UserManager:
    METHOD __init__():
        SET self.users_file = 'users.txt'
        CALL self._load_users()

    METHOD _load_users():
        INIT self.users = {}
        IF FILE EXISTS(self.users_file):
            READ FILE line by line:
                SPLIT line into username, password, email
                STORE in self.users[username] = {'password': password, 'email': email}

    METHOD register(username, password, email):
        IF username in self.users:
            RETURN False
        APPEND username|password|email to users.txt
        ADD user to self.users
        RETURN True
```
Third-Party Libraries:  
- Flask  
- os  

